 try some of that  and of course  white now has a winning tactic here so  you at home  pause the video see if you can find how  to win  uh a full piece and kind of even more  uh in one single move here so hopefully  you found it of course the idea is the  simple move queen to e2  pinning the knight to the king and  applying more pressure  and at first glance it might not seem  like it's all that bad  uh of course if black plays some sort of  naive move like d5 we're gonna hit him  with d3  attacking the pinned piece and winning  the material  but you might think why not just queen  to e7 sort of defending this knight  outright  and it looks as if you know there's  there's no serious problems yet  well once again we need another clever  move to win the game  go ahead and try to find it at home  otherwise here it is  it's the move knight d5 uh the classic  removal of the defender  and we're going to follow up with d3  next this queen simply cannot both  unpin the knight and defend the c7  square so black would have to move out  of the way  and again now we get d3 and are winning  a full piece  so uh this is why  pre-arranged draws can have some uh  unintentional consequences here  uh and i believe there's a story go  floating around on the internet about  the game between larry christensen and  anthony miles  and that is that uh anthony miles spent  a lot of time  cleaning off the e2 square adjusting it  with this finger to make sure there was  no dust there  just to show larry the folly he had made  but miles stuck to the pre-arranged  agreement  and they drew that game ending up in  vichy losing  in just six moves how embarrassing  as always thank you guys so much for  tuning in for this episode of  game review my name is caleb denby and i  will see you next time
 

